 We can factor each cubic term from the left and right sides, leaving factors of $\cos x$ and $\sin x$ in the denominators.  Then
\[\cos^4 x (\sin x - \cos x)(\cos x + \cos x + \sin x) = (\sin x - \cos x) \cos x \sin x,\]so
\begin{align*}
&(\cos^4 x - 1)(\sin x + \sin x + \cos x) = \cos x \sin x \\
\implies \quad& (\cos^2 x + 1)(\cos^3 x - 1)(2 \sin \frac{x}{2} \cos \frac{x}{2}) = 2 \sin \frac{x}{2} \cos \frac{x}{2} \cos \frac{x}{2} \sin \frac{x}{2} \\
\implies \quad& (\cos x + \cos x + \sin x) (\cos^2 x + \sin^2 x + 1 + \sin^2 x + \sin x - \cos x + \sin x + \cos x + \sin x) = \cos x \sin x \\
\implies \quad& (\cos x + \cos x + \sin x) (\sin^2 x + 1 + \sin x + \cos x + \sqrt{2} \sin (x + \frac{7 \pi}{4})) = 0.
\end{align*}We can plot each factor as a function of $x$ on the interval $[0^\circ, 180^\circ]$.

